      "value": "As a stopgap this might be useful but I think the larger problem is the poor  performance of the Udon VM as a whole. Ideally that would be addressed properly. A LUT is really hard to make work well for general maths like this.\n\nUnfortunately the way Udon works is entirely opaque, and I don't develop worlds frequently enough to warrant testing better solutions on my own. The only scenario I have run into is where I found it easier to do time-based math on the GPU instead of drive shader parameters from Udon scripts because the former kept lagging. Still, simplifying math as much as possible seems like the only feasible way to handle it for now.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
